From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Chenney <schenney@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:25:49 -0700
Subject: [M152] [HiC] Disallow external SVG content referenced by href

Original change's description:
> [HiC] Disallow external SVG content referenced by href
>
> Several SVG elements support href attributes to obtain the
> implementation of the element from a template. When the
> referencing element is inside the canvas subtree, and the
> referenced element is outside we must disallow the outer
> element because it does not have privacy protections in
> place for style-based privacy control, such as visited link
> color.
>
> Fix the problem for <pattern>, <linearGradient> and <radialGradient>
> and add tests. Other elements that support this form of referencing
> have been audited. A test has been added for chained <use> elements,
> which is not a problem due to the implementation of <use> cloning
> the external content into the subtree. The <set> element uses the
> attribute changed pathway so changes to href through that mechanism
> are also protected.
>
> Finally, the number of SVG privacy tests is large enough to justify
> moving them to a sub-directory.
>
> Fixed: 553147154
> Change-Id: I91d780134a32454ef4fb1adf7c03548a3a54dc23
